{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787201930048345001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"nonodorous-snotty-seaurchin","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"6992c2d4e0444afcd2ed15853a01d9d711e0c5dbbc64f9bf10b6cd8fb1bbdc30","event_uuid":"da6b97de-33cd-4b7b-bf57-aeccd7c6d345","position":{"commit_sha":"c4f89d65a12ce7fb16acc026ff3d10f86d7c3862","position":"1787199566442392001-da6b97de-33cd-4b7b-bf57-aeccd7c6d345"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5318113a0de8f49736e9f1171349864c7d41d6d3f513047c0a4c07335a964575","event_uuid":"ed357bec-002b-4b3a-a253-b2612178ed32","position":{"commit_sha":"95ab2bd81e6c67ea559a13e2f9beb53e0775be78","position":"1787199575402689001-ed357bec-002b-4b3a-a253-b2612178ed32"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787199566442392001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ed357bec-002b-4b3a-a253-b2612178ed32","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b4c2-db4c-fde5-4a45"}],"description":"## Report — NOT independently reproduced yet, read the caveat\nAn agent landing Gerrit 1943 reported that running pytest **detached via `nohup`** produced errors\nthat **did not reproduce in a foreground shell**:\n\n- two bpmn-io browser e2e tests, and\n- `test_partial_clone_refusal_names_fresh_unfiltered_clone_remedy`\n\nall errored under the detached run, then **passed on a foreground re-run** (12 passed / 6 passed).\nIt recorded that it \"nearly chased those as real regressions.\"\n\n**I have not reproduced this myself.** This ticket is filed to establish whether the effect is real\nand what causes it — not to assert a defect. Investigation should start by reproducing the\nforeground/detached difference on an unmodified tree before touching anything.\n\n## Why it is worth establishing rather than shrugging off\nAgents in this project routinely run the full suite detached, because a serial local run takes hours\nand exceeds tool timeouts. If a detached run reports errors a foreground run does not, then the\ncheap validation path produces false positives, and the expensive path is the only trustworthy one.\nTwo costs follow:\n\n1. **Wasted investigation.** At least one agent nearly root-caused phantom regressions. Time spent\n   chasing an artifact is time not spent on the actual change.\n2. **Erosion of the signal.** The dangerous direction is the inverse of (1): once \"errors in the\n   detached run are probably spurious\" becomes folklore, a REAL regression in a detached run gets\n   waved through with the same shrug. That is the same failure mode the withdrawn ticket\n   `bitesized-fluorite-aruanas` warned about for `tests/interfaces` — dismissing a class of failure\n   by reputation rather than by diagnosis.\n\n## Distinguish this from a KNOWN and different artifact\nSeveral agents this session reported errors in long background runs that were **self-inflicted and\nfully explained**: the run raced the agent's own `git commit` / `git reset --hard` / branch switch in\nthe same worktree, and repo-hygiene guards fired with messages naming the exact HEAD move (e.g.\n\"Test moved the repo HEAD (a9cbc2d34e -> 74daf58e52)\"). Those are not this. They are correct guards\ncatching a genuinely mutating tree.\n\nThe report here is different in kind: no HEAD move was implicated, and the same commit passed\nforeground. Investigation must not conflate the two — establishing which of the reported errors\nbelong to which class is itself part of the work.\n\n## Candidate mechanisms to discriminate between\n- Process-group / TTY differences under `nohup` (browser e2e tests in particular may need a session\n  or display that a detached process lacks).\n- Working-directory or environment differences between the detached process and the foreground shell.\n- Resource contention: a detached full-tree run may overlap other work in a way a foreground run does\n  not, hitting timeouts that read as errors.\n- Harness reaping: a detached runner being partially killed and its teardown reported as errors.\n\nThe bpmn-io **browser** e2e tests are the strongest lead — a browser harness is exactly the kind of\nthing that behaves differently without a controlling terminal.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The foreground/detached difference is either REPRODUCED on an unmodified tree, or shown not to\n      reproduce — with the exact invocations for both runs recorded so a later reader can repeat them.\n- [ ] If it reproduces, each affected test is classified: genuinely environment-dependent (and why),\n      versus a real defect the detached run exposes. Do not stop at \"spurious.\"\n- [ ] The reported errors are separated from the KNOWN self-inflicted HEAD-move class, so the two are\n      not conflated in whatever guidance results.\n- [ ] Whatever the outcome, the recommended way for an agent to validate the whole tree locally is\n      recorded in `docs/local-dev-env.md` — including whether detached runs are trustworthy, and if\n      not, what to do instead given a serial run exceeds tool timeouts.\n- [ ] If specific tests genuinely cannot run detached, they SKIP with an explicit reason in that mode\n      rather than erroring, so a detached run's error output stays meaningful.\n\n## Provenance\nReported 2026-08-20 by the agent on ticket `visionary-pernicious-ynambu` (Gerrit 1943, merged), which\nrecorded it as a method note rather than absorbing it. Filed here so it is investigated rather than\nbecoming folklore.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f0fb-de7a-b315-4508","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Detached (nohup) pytest runs report errors that do not reproduce in a foreground shell","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["da6b97de-33cd-4b7b-bf57-aeccd7c6d345","ed357bec-002b-4b3a-a253-b2612178ed32"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787201930048345001,"uuid":"170467b5-8872-43f1-8d73-e9db6779058f"}